From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: handle ThinkSmart stock firmware init and bufferless EOS

The Lenovo stock firmware advertises 76 system-init properties, with
zero padding and an incomplete encoder capability beyond the counted
response. Its downstream parser treats adjacent codec-support and
max-session records as one property. Validate that pair and complete
variable arrays, stop at the advertised count, and report surplus bytes.

The same firmware can send a decoder EOS completion with no buffer
address or valid tag. Do not mistake its dummy tag zero for capture
buffer zero. Defer LAST/event completion to work outside the firmware IRQ
thread; retain EOS until a driver-owned capture buffer becomes available.
Track firmware output ownership and readonly references so synthetic LAST
and same-FD restart cannot steal or duplicate firmware-owned buffers.
Cancel work during teardown and reset ownership after confirmed flushes.

Also accept a successful, empty EOS for the client-visible output whose
tag no longer identifies a queued capture buffer, even when its address
is nonzero. Keep the addressless interception before tag lookup to avoid
mistaking dummy tag zero for a real buffer. Reuse the same deferred,
one-shot completion path; do not flush or steal firmware-owned buffers.
Error, corrupt, dropped, nonempty and internal-DPB returns do not enter
the additional fallback.

Enable both compatibility quirks only on lenovo,cd-18781y with
qcom,msm8953-venus. Other boards retain their existing parsing and EOF
paths, with additional bounds validation for variable arrays.

Retain Linux 7.3's upstream capability/allocation payload-size fixes.
Its raw-format structures contain a single trailing plane record rather
than flexible arrays, so validate each variable-length wire record using
its field offsets and accumulate the actual bytes consumed.

This compatibility behavior was exercised on the earlier 7.1 kernel,
including exact-pixel H.264/HEVC decoding, deferred EOF, command restart,
STREAMOFF pool reuse and drain cancellation. On Linux 7.3, H.264 High with
B-frames and HEVC with and without B-frames retained exact software-decoded
pixels through drain, command restart and STREAMOFF pool reuse. Those runs
do not establish that the additional nonzero-address missing-tag fallback
was exercised, or renew the earlier drain-cancellation qualification.
This is not a firmware-version-independent policy.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
Reference: https://github.com/jethac/lenovo-thinksmart-view/blob/fe9c0a58a1a2b7c4893f2ff76ff5c0b90206d458/kernel/patches/0703-media-venus-vdec-deliver-an-EOS-the-firmware-signals-on-a-returned-buffer.patch
Adaptation: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>; extend the existing EOS
  mechanism for missing-tag completions, without importing the reference's
  asynchronous output-flush implementation or any encoder changes.
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7
Apply in filename order within this project.


---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index e040397acdf3349912778475e29d63ac9d327d96..67a728320c3f14830409f72ea073f72ab0e805d8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -409,6 +409,11 @@ static int venus_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!core->res)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,msm8953-venus") &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,cd-18781y"))
+		core->quirks = VENUS_QUIRK_LEGACY_SYS_INIT |
+			       VENUS_QUIRK_BUFFERLESS_EOS;
+
 	mutex_init(&core->pm_lock);
 
 	core->pm_ops = venus_pm_get(core->res->hfi_version);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
